      "sourceTextSha256": "8b73ea11cd64c2d24c9dc7db17b39b02291dd564b5cbb6d260f7824d189040e1",
      "text": "Day 6 · After breakfast, discover a region famous for hiking, rivers, waterfalls and natural pools. Maringá is its main village, with shops and restaurants, and Vila de Maromba is known as the village of waterfalls. Your driver takes you into a protected natural area where an easy hike reveals a series of up to 12 waterfalls, a garden of Eden of falling water, flowers and great trees; Brazilians believe that bathing in waterfalls cleanses both body and soul. The most popular is the Escorrega waterfall, with a natural pool and a natural rock slide. Optional activities include climbing, horseback riding and hiking.",
